When a demo output is a dense repeating field but other examples look unlike it, neither force a shared rule from visual similarity nor dismiss the periodic case as unrelated. Treat the pattern as a testable abstraction: record the output's row/column period, color cycle ordering, direction, and phase/origin; compare these with the input's sparse diagonal tracks, marker sequence, or stripe ordering. Distinguish period from phase (a correct cycle with wrong origin still fails exact replay).

Replay the proposed generator against every complete demo. Include cases where the output is uniform or striped: these may be degenerate instances of a shared periodic generator, or evidence against it, and must not be ignored. A test input that visually resembles a periodic encoding only motivates the hypothesis; it does not establish mapping. If no deterministic cycle/phase rule reproduces all outputs, label it unresolved rather than submitting cosmetic rotations/reversals or repeatedly requesting demos without a discriminating prediction.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u075/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-ledger/references/periodic-field-cross-demo-test.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-delta-discipline", "file": "references/marker-anchor-offsets.md", "content": "# Marker-to-template anchor offsets

When demos show sparse markers receiving copies of an embedded motif, keep two coordinate concepts separate: (1) the motif's bounding-box origin and (2) the motif coordinate that aligns with a marker. Represent the latter as a signed offset from the origin and validate it against multiple marker/copy pairs. A plausible colored pattern is not enough: replay every marker footprint against the complete output, including the original motif, overlaps, clipping, and unchanged candidate markers.

A repeated failure mode is to shift the right motif by an intuitively appealing amount (top-left, center, a nearby marker, or a visually salient source pixel) without validating the anchor. On incorrect feedback, discard that placement hypothesis and derive the offset anew from observed coordinate correspondences. Also validate serialization independently: every row must have the expected width and all values must be legal before submitting.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u075/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-delta-discipline/references/marker-anchor-offsets.md"}

